    <statement><p>An aluminum can is to be constructed to contain 2100 <m>cm^3</m> of liquid.</p>
<p>Let <m>r</m> and <m>h</m> be the radius of the base and the height of the can
respectively.</p>
<p>a) Express <m>h</m> in terms of <m>r</m>. (If needed you can enter <m>\pi</m> as pi.)</p>
<p><m>h =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>b) Express the surface area of the can in terms of <m>r</m>.</p>
<p>Surface area = <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>c) Approximate the value of <m>r</m> that will minimize the amount of
required material (i.e. the value of <m>r</m> that will minimize the surface area).</p>
<p>What is the corresponding value of <m>h</m>?</p>
<p><m>r =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>h =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2100}{3.14159r^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.28319r^{2}+\frac{4200}{r}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.93979234383925</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>13.8795846876785</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
